# Arena and Level Design

Status: NOT_STARTED
Milestone: M2 Vertical slice
Dependencies: pressure decision in `15_PRODUCT_DECISIONS.todo`, `04_TERRITORY_PAINTING.todo`

## Purpose

Build one original gray-box arena that supports routes, contests, reactions, bot navigation, and a readable
match climax.

## Tasks

- [ ] Define arena metrics.
- [ ] Define spawn safety.
- [ ] Define paintable and non-paintable surfaces.
- [ ] Create primary, alternate, and comeback routes.
- [ ] Create central contest space.
- [ ] Integrate selected pressure mechanism.
- [ ] Add bot navigation.
- [ ] Add camera-collision validation.
- [ ] Add out-of-bounds handling.
- [ ] Add ownership/debug visualization.
- [ ] Run route and sightline review.
- [ ] Run full-match gray-box playtest.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] No spawn has an obvious structural advantage.
- [ ] Players can identify at least two meaningful routes.
- [ ] Pressure produces conflict without unavoidable trapping.
- [ ] Bot can reach all intended contest zones.
- [ ] Camera remains usable throughout the arena.
- [ ] Territory coverage does not reward inaccessible surfaces.

